      "index": 102,
      "start": 261.239,
      "end": 262.87,
      "duration": 1.631,
      "text": "minus two"
    },
    {
      "index": 103,
      "start": 262.88,
      "end": 264.27,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "u"
    },
    {
      "index": 104,
      "start": 264.28,
      "end": 266.55,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "t minus one."
    },
    {
      "index": 105,
      "start": 266.56,
      "end": 268.75,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "So, just to remind you here"
    },
    {
      "index": 106,
      "start": 268.76,
      "end": 270.87,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "of what u of t is are, just want to"
    },
    {
      "index": 107,
      "start": 270.88,
      "end": 272.87,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "sketch"
    },
    {
      "index": 108,
      "start": 272.88,
      "end": 274.91,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "a few things."
    },
    {
      "index": 109,
      "start": 274.92,
      "end": 276.75,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "So, first"
    },
    {
      "index": 110,
      "start": 276.76,
      "end": 278.39,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "u of t is just a step function that"
    },
    {
      "index": 111,
      "start": 278.4,
      "end": 280.31,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "would be zero everywhere and would take"
    },
    {
      "index": 112,
      "start": 280.32,
      "end": 283.27,
      "duration": 2.95,
      "text": "the value one for t larger than zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 113,
      "start": 283.28,
      "end": 284.95,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "So, this first part here would just be"
    },
    {
      "index": 114,
      "start": 284.96,
      "end": 287.43,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "non-zero for t larger than zero. Instead"
    },
    {
      "index": 115,
      "start": 287.44,
      "end": 289.19,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "of being assigned value one, it's just"
    },
    {
      "index": 116,
      "start": 289.2,
      "end": 290.75,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "be assigned value three cuz we're"
    },
    {
      "index": 117,
      "start": 290.76,
      "end": 293.83,
      "duration": 3.07,
      "text": "multiplying the u of t by three."
    },
    {
      "index": 118,
      "start": 293.84,
      "end": 296.43,
      "duration": 2.59,
      "text": "So, this first part would look like"
    },
    {
      "index": 119,
      "start": 296.44,
      "end": 297.79,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "this."
    },
    {
      "index": 120,
      "start": 297.8,
      "end": 300.71,
      "duration": 2.91,
      "text": "The second part here would be u shifted"
    },
    {
      "index": 121,
      "start": 300.72,
      "end": 301.91,
      "duration": 1.19,
      "text": "to t"
    },
    {
      "index": 122,
      "start": 301.92,
      "end": 305.47,
      "duration": 3.55,
      "text": "t by by minus one, which means that u"
    },
    {
      "index": 123,
      "start": 305.48,
      "end": 308.63,
      "duration": 3.15,
      "text": "is zero everywhere for t less than one."
    },
    {
      "index": 124,
      "start": 308.64,
      "end": 310.51,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "So, you would have zero function here."
    },
    {
      "index": 125,
      "start": 310.52,
      "end": 313.23,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "So, let me just do dots."
    },
    {
      "index": 126,
      "start": 313.24,
      "end": 315.95,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "But, it should be on the same axis and"
    },
    {
      "index": 127,
      "start": 315.96,
      "end": 318.71,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "one for t larger than one. But, here"
    },
    {
      "index": 128,
      "start": 318.72,
      "end": 320.55,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "we're giving it a multiplying it by"
    },
    {
      "index": 129,
      "start": 320.56,
      "end": 322.55,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "factor minus two. So, really what we"
    },
    {
      "index": 130,
      "start": 322.56,
      "end": 325.91,
      "duration": 3.35,
      "text": "have"
    },
    {
      "index": 131,
      "start": 331.91,
      "end": 331.92,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "function that is shifted down"
    },
    {
      "index": 132,
      "start": 331.92,
      "end": 333.99,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "to minus two. So, the sum of these two"
    },
    {
      "index": 133,
      "start": 334.0,
      "end": 336.47,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "contributions"
    },
    {
      "index": 134,
      "start": 336.48,
      "end": 338.91,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "is zero for t negative"
    },
    {
      "index": 135,
      "start": 338.92,
      "end": 340.71,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "takes the value three"
    },
    {
      "index": 136,
      "start": 340.72,
      "end": 344.11,
      "duration": 3.39,
      "text": "for t between zero and one"
    },
    {
      "index": 137,
      "start": 344.12,
      "end": 345.91,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "and the value one"
    },
    {
      "index": 138,
      "start": 345.92,
      "end": 347.43,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "three minus two"
    },
    {
      "index": 139,
      "start": 347.44,
      "end": 349.23,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "for"
    },
    {
      "index": 140,
      "start": 349.24,
      "end": 352.15,
      "duration": 2.91,
      "text": "t larger than one, okay? So, clearly"
    },
    {
      "index": 141,
      "start": 352.16,
      "end": 354.11,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "here we have discontinuities at t equals"
    },
    {
      "index": 142,
      "start": 354.12,
      "end": 355.99,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "to zero and t equals to one."
    },
    {
      "index": 143,
      "start": 356.0,
      "end": 356.95,
      "duration": 0.95,
      "text": "So, let's just write down the"
    },
    {
      "index": 144,
      "start": 356.96,
      "end": 359.23,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "derivative."
    },
    {
      "index": 145,
      "start": 359.24,
      "end": 361.35,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "The generalized derivative here"
    },
    {
      "index": 146,
      "start": 361.36,
      "end": 362.67,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "would lead us first to compute the"
    },
    {
      "index": 147,
      "start": 362.68,
      "end": 364.35,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "derivatives when"
    },
    {
      "index": 148,
      "start": 364.36,
      "end": 366.35,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "where the function is continuous. So,"
    },
    {
      "index": 149,
      "start": 366.36,
      "end": 368.19,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "from minus infinity to zero it's a"
    },
    {
      "index": 150,
      "start": 368.2,
      "end": 370.23,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "constant, so derivative would be zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 151,
      "start": 370.24,
      "end": 372.43,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "Between zero and one it's constant,"
    },
    {
      "index": 152,
      "start": 372.44,
      "end": 374.31,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "derivative would be zero. And from one"
    },
    {
      "index": 153,
      "start": 374.32,
      "end": 376.35,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "to infinity it would also give us zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 154,
      "start": 376.36,
      "end": 377.91,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "So, we would have a zero contribution"
    },
    {
      "index": 155,
      "start": 377.92,
      "end": 379.79,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "from the the continuous part of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 156,
      "start": 379.8,
      "end": 381.35,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "function if you wish."
    },
    {
      "index": 157,
      "start": 381.36,
      "end": 382.91,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "But, we still need to account for the"
    },
    {
      "index": 158,
      "start": 382.92,
      "end": 384.95,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "discontinuities. So, at zero we have a"
    },
    {
      "index": 159,
      "start": 384.96,
      "end": 387.31,
      "duration": 2.35,
      "text": "jump from zero to three and that we"
    },
    {
      "index": 160,
      "start": 387.32,
      "end": 390.03,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "learned can be written down as a delta"
    },
    {
      "index": 161,
      "start": 390.04,
      "end": 392.03,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "function"
    },
    {
      "index": 162,
      "start": 392.04,
      "end": 395.71,
      "duration": 3.67,
      "text": "of magnitude three centered at zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 163,
      "start": 395.72,
      "end": 397.51,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "After that we have another jump. Now,"
    },
    {
      "index": 164,
      "start": 397.52,
      "end": 399.43,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "it's from three to one. So, it's a jump"
    },
    {
      "index": 165,
      "start": 399.44,
      "end": 402.63,
      "duration": 3.19,
      "text": "of minus two amplitude centered at one."
    },
    {
      "index": 166,
      "start": 402.64,
      "end": 404.59,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "So, here we can also do that with the"
    },
    {
      "index": 167,
      "start": 404.6,
      "end": 406.79,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "delta, but we just need also to shift it"
    },
    {
      "index": 168,
      "start": 406.8,
      "end": 409.23,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "by minus one to to show clearly that the"
    },
    {
      "index": 169,
      "start": 409.24,
      "end": 411.11,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "jump occurs at one"
    },
    {
      "index": 170,
      "start": 411.12,
      "end": 414.15,
      "duration": 3.03,
      "text": "and multiply this by minus two to show"
    },
    {
      "index": 171,
      "start": 414.16,
      "end": 417.07,
      "duration": 2.91,
      "text": "the amplitude of the jump down, okay?"
    },
    {
      "index": 172,
      "start": 417.08,
      "end": 418.99,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "So, if we were now to represent it f"
    },
    {
      "index": 173,
      "start": 419.0,
      "end": 422.79,
      "duration": 3.79,
      "text": "prime"
    },
    {
      "index": 174,
      "start": 424.67,
      "end": 424.68,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "basically the regular part zero, so"
    },
    {
      "index": 175,
      "start": 424.68,
      "end": 426.15,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "there's nothing to"
    },
    {
      "index": 176,
      "start": 426.16,
      "end": 427.51,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "to write down except just a zero"
    },
    {
      "index": 177,
      "start": 427.52,
      "end": 430.35,
      "duration": 2.83,
      "text": "function and the discontinuities that"
    },
    {
      "index": 178,
      "start": 430.36,
      "end": 432.75,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "I'm just going to represent on the graph"
    },
    {
      "index": 179,
      "start": 432.76,
      "end": 434.71,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "would be the delta function"
    },
    {
      "index": 180,
      "start": 434.72,
      "end": 438.67,
      "duration": 3.95,
      "text": "centered at zero of magnitude three."
    },
    {
      "index": 181,
      "start": 441.75,
      "end": 441.76,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And delta function centered around one"
    },
    {
      "index": 182,
      "start": 441.76,
      "end": 444.91,
      "duration": 3.15,
      "text": "of magnitude minus two."
    },
    {
      "index": 183,
      "start": 444.92,
      "end": 446.87,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "And the rest would just be the zero"
    },
    {
      "index": 184,
      "start": 446.88,
      "end": 449.19,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "function."
    },
    {
      "index": 185,
      "start": 449.2,
      "end": 452.87,
      "duration": 3.67,
      "text": "So, that would be f prime."
    },
    {
      "index": 186,
      "start": 455.07,
      "end": 455.08,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "That's f of t."
    },
    {
      "index": 187,
      "start": 455.08,
      "end": 460.23,
      "duration": 5.15,
      "text": "So, for the second one"
    },
    {
      "index": 188,
      "start": 462.19,
      "end": 462.2,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "that we were given"
    },
    {
      "index": 189,
      "start": 462.2,
      "end": 465.07,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "it's a function f of t"
    },
    {
      "index": 190,
      "start": 465.08,
      "end": 467.55,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "that takes the value t squared"
    },
    {
      "index": 191,
      "start": 467.56,
      "end": 469.11,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "for t negative"
    },
    {
      "index": 192,
      "start": 469.12,
      "end": 471.07,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "and exponential"
    },
    {
      "index": 193,
      "start": 471.08,
      "end": 474.75,
      "duration": 3.67,
      "text": "minus t"
    },
    {
      "index": 194,
      "start": 476.87,
      "end": 476.88,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "for t positive."
    },
    {
      "index": 195,
      "start": 476.88,
      "end": 478.87,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "So, quick sketch here"
    },
    {
      "index": 196,
      "start": 478.88,
      "end": 480.91,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "tells that this function looks like this"
    },
    {
      "index": 197,
      "start": 480.92,
      "end": 483.43,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "an exponential minus t"
    },
    {
      "index": 198,
      "start": 483.44,
      "end": 485.71,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "for t positive, okay?"
    },
    {
      "index": 199,
      "start": 485.72,
      "end": 487.51,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "Taking a value here one. So, clearly"
    },
    {
      "index": 200,
      "start": 487.52,
      "end": 489.83,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "there is a jump here."
    },
    {
      "index": 201,
      "start": 489.84,
      "end": 491.67,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "Discontinuity."
    },
    {
      "index": 202,
      "start": 491.68,
      "end": 494.07,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "So, how do we go about computing this"
    },
    {
      "index": 203,
      "start": 494.08,
      "end": 495.99,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "generalized derivative? So, let's look"
    },
    {
      "index": 204,
      "start": 496.0,
      "end": 498.75,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "again at the continuous parts. So, from"
    },
    {
      "index": 205,
      "start": 498.76,
      "end": 500.71,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "minus infinity to zero we're dealing"
    },
    {
      "index": 206,
      "start": 500.72,
      "end": 502.43,
      "duration": 1.71,
      "text": "with just a t squared. So, the"
    },
    {
      "index": 207,
      "start": 502.44,
      "end": 506.71,
      "duration": 4.27,
      "text": "derivative is just 2t."
    },
    {
      "index": 208,
      "start": 508.51,
      "end": 508.52,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "For t between zero and infinity we're"
    },
    {
      "index": 209,
      "start": 508.52,
      "end": 510.75,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "just dealing with exponential minus t."
    },
    {
      "index": 210,
      "start": 510.76,
      "end": 515.589,
      "duration": 4.829,
      "text": "So, that's minus exponential minus t."
    },
    {
      "index": 211,
      "start": 516.79,
      "end": 516.8,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "But, we need to account for the"
    },
    {
      "index": 212,
      "start": 516.8,
      "end": 519.99,
      "duration": 3.19,
      "text": "discontinuity, the jump of amplitude one"
    },
    {
      "index": 213,
      "start": 520.0,
      "end": 522.55,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "at zero. So, as we saw before this can"
    },
    {
      "index": 214,
      "start": 522.56,
      "end": 524.71,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "just be modeled"
    },
    {
      "index": 215,
      "start": 524.72,
      "end": 526.75,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "with a delta function."
    },
    {
      "index": 216,
      "start": 526.76,
      "end": 528.07,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "And if we were to represent this"
    },
    {
      "index": 217,
      "start": 528.08,
      "end": 531.71,
      "duration": 3.63,
      "text": "function, then we would just need"
    },
    {
      "index": 218,
      "start": 531.72,
      "end": 534.95,
      "duration": 3.23,
      "text": "to add a delta function"
    },
    {
      "index": 219,
      "start": 534.96,
      "end": 537.71,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "of magnitude one here and then just"
    },
    {
      "index": 220,
      "start": 537.72,
      "end": 541.83,
      "duration": 4.11,
      "text": "sketch 2t. So, for for example"
    },
    {
      "index": 221,
      "start": 541.84,
      "end": 546.43,
      "duration": 4.59,
      "text": "and then minus exponential minus 2t."
    },
    {
      "index": 222,
      "start": 546.44,
      "end": 548.39,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "That would give us something like that."
    },
    {
      "index": 223,
      "start": 548.4,
      "end": 550.71,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "And that ends the problem for today. And"
    },
    {
      "index": 224,
      "start": 550.72,
      "end": 552.27,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "the key points here were just to learn"
    },
    {
      "index": 225,
      "start": 552.28,
      "end": 555.95,
      "duration": 3.67,
      "text": "how to manipulate the the step function"
    },
    {
      "index": 226,
      "start": 555.96,
      "end": 558.83,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "and how to use the delta function when"
    },
    {
      "index": 227,
      "start": 558.84,
      "end": 560.39,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "you compute your integrals and be"
    },
    {
      "index": 228,
      "start": 560.4,
      "end": 564.12,
      "duration": 3.72,
      "text": "careful with the bounds of integration."
    }
  ],
  "course": {
    "category": "Mathematics",
    "title": "Differential Equations",
    "source_url": "https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL64BDFBDA2AF24F7E"
  }
